#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:455
msgid "Red Hat: <literal>./autogen.sh</literal> and wait while it compiles"
msgstr ""
"Red Hat: kör <literal>./autogen.sh</literal> och vänta medan programmet "
"kompileras"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:459
msgid ""
"<emphasis role=\"bold\">Optional:</emphasis> <emphasis>$root</emphasis> "
"<literal>make install</literal>"
msgstr ""
"<emphasis role=\"bold\">Valfritt:</emphasis> <emphasis>$root</emphasis> "
"<literal>make install</literal>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:460
msgid ""
"If you find that this didn't work, try <literal>make clean</literal> and "
"then repeat from the autogen step. For example, sometimes I've had it not "
"create the python-loader."
msgstr ""
"Om det inte fungerade kan du prova <literal>make clean</literal> och sedan "
"upprepa stegen från autogen-steget. Ibland har jag till exempel varit med om"
" att python-loader inte skapades."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:468
msgid ""
"OK, you should now have gnumeric! Test it! If you installed the Debianized "
"version via apt-get, or did \"make install\", it should be installed to "
"/usr/bin (or /usr/local/bin on Red Hat?) and you can just type "
"<literal>gnumeric</literal>. Otherwise you will find it in "
"<literal>gnumeric-head/src/</literal> and you will have to run it from "
"there."
msgstr ""
"Nu bör du ha Gnumeric! Testa programmet. Om du installerade Debianpaketet "
"med apt-get eller körde ”make install” ska programmet finnas i /usr/bin "
"(eller /usr/local/bin på Red Hat?). Starta det med kommandot "
"<literal>gnumeric</literal>. Annars finns programmet i <literal>gnumeric-"
"head/src/</literal> och måste köras därifrån."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:486
msgid "The Python Console"
msgstr "Python-konsolen"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:488
msgid ""
"There is an interactive Python console available from inside Gnumeric. This "
"is a good place to explore things, and if the console is expanded, will be a"
" nice place for scripting. In the meantime, what I have called "
"\"Spellbooks\" below are much more useful, but are fixed plugins as of "
"Gnumeric startup. So right now I putter in the console as I develop plugin "
"literal in the form of spellbooks. After 1.2.0, Gnumeric will be working on "
"its scripting API, so the two approaches may merge. Or not."
msgstr ""
"Gnumeric har en interaktiv Python-konsol. Där kan du utforska programmet, "
"och om konsolen byggs ut blir den en bra plats för skript. Än så länge är de"
" ”magiböcker” jag beskriver nedan mer användbara, men de är fasta "
"insticksmoduler som laddas när Gnumeric startar. Under tiden experimenterar "
"jag i konsolen medan jag utvecklar insticksmoduler i form av magiböcker. "
"Efter version 1.2.0 ska Gnumeric få ett skript-API, så de två sätten kanske "
"kan slås ihop. Eller inte."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:500
msgid "Enabling the Python Console"
msgstr "Aktivera Python-konsolen"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:502
msgid ""
"You can run a Python interpreter from inside Gnumeric, but you have to turn "
"it on. To do this you simply uncomment a line in python-loader/plugins.xml. "
"Normally, that file lives in "
"/usr/lib/gnumeric/<emphasis>$version</emphasis>/plugins/python-loader/, or "
"perhaps <emphasis>/usr/local/lib...</emphasis> on Red Hat. I used to suggest"
" making a local but you should probably make a local copy, but that was pain"
" for little gain. So:"
msgstr ""
"Du kan köra en Python-tolk inifrån Gnumeric, men först måste du aktivera "
"den. Ta bort kommentarstecknen framför en rad i python-loader/plugins.xml. "
"Filen finns vanligtvis i "
"/usr/lib/gnumeric/<emphasis>$version</emphasis>/plugins/python-loader/ eller"
" kanske under <emphasis>/usr/local/lib...</emphasis> i Red Hat. Tidigare "
"föreslog jag att skapa en lokal kopia, men det extra arbetet ger nog inte så"
" mycket. Gör så här:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:515
msgid ""
"<literal>gnumeric --version</literal> to make sure you get the right version"
" name for the following. (You'll have to do this for every new version of "
"Gnumeric!)"
msgstr ""
"Kör <literal>gnumeric --version</literal> för att ta reda på rätt "
"versionsnamn nedan. Du behöver göra detta för varje ny Gnumeric-version"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:523
msgid ""
"<literal>cd ~/.gnumeric/</literal> <emphasis>$version</emphasis> "
"<literal>/plugins/</literal>"
msgstr ""
"<literal>cd ~/.gnumeric/</literal> <emphasis>$version</emphasis> "
"<literal>/plugins/</literal>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:531
msgid "Edit <literal>python-loader/plugin.xml</literal>."
msgstr "Redigera <literal>python-loader/plugin.xml</literal>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:537
msgid ""
"Uncomment the five lines starting with <literal>ui-console-menu "
"service</literal> near the bottom (remove the \"&lt;!--\" and \"--&gt;\" "
"tags around the &lt;service...&gt; and &lt;/service&gt; tags."
msgstr ""
"Ta bort kommentaren runt de fem raderna som börjar med <literal>ui-console-"
"menu service</literal> nära slutet av filen (ta bort taggarna ”&lt;!--” och "
"”--&gt;” runt taggarna &lt;service...&gt; och &lt;/service&gt;)."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:552
msgid "Start gnumeric (same version)."
msgstr "Starta gnumeric (samma version)."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:558
msgid ""
"Select from the <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> the <guimenuitem>Python "
"console</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""
"Välj <guimenu>Verktyg</guimenu> och sedan <guimenuitem>Python-"
"konsol</guimenuitem>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:565
msgid "<emphasis>Enjoy!</emphasis>"
msgstr "<emphasis>Njut!</emphasis>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:575
msgid "Playing with the Python console"
msgstr "Utforska Python-konsolen"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:577
msgid ""
"At the top there is a drop-down menu <guimenu>Execute in</guimenu>. Right "
"now your only choice will be <guimenuitem>Default</guimenuitem>. After you "
"evaluate functions from other plugins, those environments will become "
"available too (JK says this is called lazy loading). But I'll assume you are"
" using Default. (The only real difference is that you have to import "
"Gnumeric first, and you can't see your plugin functions.)"
msgstr ""
"Längst upp finns listrutan <guimenu>Exekvera i</guimenu>. Till att börja med"
" är <guimenuitem>Standard</guimenuitem> det enda alternativet. När du har "
"kört funktioner från andra insticksmoduler blir även deras miljöer "
"tillgängliga (JK kallar detta ”lazy loading”). Jag utgår från att du "
"använder Standard. Den enda egentliga skillnaden är att du måste importera "
"Gnumeric först och inte kan se funktionerna i dina insticksmoduler"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:588
msgid ""
"(Note: older releases required you to type <literal>print dir()</literal> "
"instead of just <literal>dir()</literal>. Fixed in cvs 16 June 2003, and "
"certainly in 1.1.20 and higher."
msgstr ""
"(Obs! I äldre versioner behövde du skriva <literal>print dir()</literal> i "
"stället för bara <literal>dir()</literal>. Detta rättades i CVS den 16 juni "
"2003 och finns definitivt i version 1.1.20 och senare."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:595
msgid "Let's start by taking a look at the environment."
msgstr "Vi börjar med att undersöka miljön."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:613
msgid ""
"'Gnumeric' is a module that exists only within Gnumeric, and which defines "
"the Gnumeric Python API."
msgstr ""
"”Gnumeric” är en modul som bara finns inifrån Gnumeric och som definierar "
"Gnumerics Python-API."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:620
msgid ""
"Gnumeric.functions is the list of all the Gnumeric functions you would see "
"in the function browser. You cannot yet do "
"<literal>dir(Gnumeric.functions)</literal> but maybe someone will bind that "
"soon."
msgstr ""
"Gnumeric.functions är en lista över alla Gnumeric-funktioner som visas i "
"funktionsbläddraren. Du kan ännu inte köra "
"<literal>dir(Gnumeric.functions)</literal>, men kanske lägger någon till det"
" snart."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:627
msgid ""
"RangeRef is not listed. That seems to limit us, though later in the tutorial"
" we'll see how to use regular functions to get inside RangeRefs."
msgstr ""
"RangeRef finns inte med i listan. Det verkar begränsa vad vi kan göra, men "
"senare i handledningen visas hur vanliga funktioner kan användas för att "
"komma åt RangeRef-objekt."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:636
msgid ""
"So do some exploring. First, let's poke around to figure out how to use "
"CellPos."
msgstr "Utforska vidare. Börja med att ta reda på hur CellPos fungerar."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:686
msgid ""
"If you evaluate in the context of a plugin (rather than in Default), then "
"<literal>dir(Gnumeric.plugin_info)</literal> will reveal some simple "
"informational functions you can call for the local plugin(s)."
msgstr ""
"Om du kör kommandot i en insticksmoduls miljö i stället för i Standard visar"
" <literal>dir(Gnumeric.plugin_info)</literal> några enkla "
"informationsfunktioner för den lokala insticksmodulen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:691
msgid ""
"Note: obviously I don't really know what I'm doing, or I wouldn't be poking "
"around like this."
msgstr ""
"Obs! Jag vet uppenbarligen inte riktigt vad jag gör, annars skulle jag inte "
"utforska på det här sättet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:697
msgid "More fun with the Python console"
msgstr "Fler saker att göra i Python-konsolen"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:699
msgid ""
"Jon K. Hellan writes, \"Here are some more things you can do from the "
"console:\""
msgstr ""
"Jon K. Hellan skriver: ”Här är några fler saker du kan göra i konsolen:”"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:736
msgid ""
"Very, very nice. Note, after setting a value, it won't show up until that "
"cell is redrawn. That will happen automatically with plugin functions, but "
"in the console, you may have to click on the cell."
msgstr ""
"När du har ändrat ett värde visas det inte förrän cellen ritas om. "
"Insticksmodulsfunktioner gör detta automatiskt, men i konsolen kan du behöva"
" klicka på cellen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:745
msgid "Using the built-in Python functions"
msgstr "Använd de inbyggda Python-funktionerna"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:747
msgid "To enable the Python-loader and Python plugins:"
msgstr "Så här aktiverar du Python-loadern och Python-insticksmodulerna:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:754
msgid ""
"Select the <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> menu and the "
"<guimenuitem>Plugins</guimenuitem> menuitem."
msgstr ""
"Välj menyn <guimenu>Verktyg</guimenu> och menyobjektet "
"<guimenuitem>Insticksmoduler</guimenuitem>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:761
msgid "Select \"Python plugin loader\" and \"Python functions\". Restart Gnumeric."
msgstr ""
"Markera ”Python-insticksmodulernas inläsare” och ”Python-funktioner”. Starta"
" om Gnumeric."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:769
msgid ""
"The quickest way to test whether you now have Python functions is to type "
"<literal>=py_capwords(\"fred flintstone\")</literal> in the first cell. "
"After you hit &lt;Enter&gt;, you should see \"Fred Flintstone\"."
msgstr ""
"Det snabbaste sättet att kontrollera om Python-funktionerna är aktiverade är"
" att skriva <literal>=py_capwords(\"fred flintstone\")</literal> i den "
"första cellen. Tryck på &lt;Enter&gt;. Då ska resultatet ”Fred Flintstone” "
"visas."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:774
msgid ""
"You can also click on the functions button, and scroll down to the "
"\"Python\" category. Select that. You should see at least two functions "
"defined: PY_CAPWORDS and PY_PRINTF. They're not very useful, but they prove "
"you've got the plugins. Test them either via the GUI or by typing into the "
"cell."
msgstr ""
"Du kan också klicka på funktionsknappen och rulla ned till kategorin "
"”Python”. Där bör det finnas minst två funktioner: PY_CAPWORDS och "
"PY_PRINTF. De är inte särskilt användbara, men visar att insticksmodulerna "
"fungerar. Testa dem i gränssnittet eller genom att skriva i en cell."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:780
msgid "I'll presume they worked."
msgstr "Jag utgår från att det fungerade."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:784
msgid "Writing your own Python functions"
msgstr "Skriv egna Python-funktioner"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:796
msgid "Transformations: of obvious value for a spreadsheet"
msgstr "Förvandlingar: självklart användbart i ett kalkylblad"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:797
msgid "Illusions: statistical functions, clearly"
msgstr "Illusioner: statistiska funktioner, förstås"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:798
msgid "Charms: presentation graphics"
msgstr "Trolleri: presentationsgrafik"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:799
msgid "Necromancy: file repair and missing values?"
msgstr "Nekromanti: filreparation och saknade värden?"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:800
msgid "Divination: data mining!"
msgstr "Spådom: datautvinning!"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:786
msgid ""
"To scribe new magic you must write your spells in places where Gnumeric will"
" find them. That place is in folders under: "
"<literal>~/.gnumeric/&lt;version&gt;/plugins/</literal> Each folder under "
"here is one \"spellbook\" of new plugin functions. You may put all your "
"spells in one spellbook, or group them neatly depending on your tastes. Each"
" spellbook must have two files. We'll create a spellbook called \"myfuncs\"."
" A pedestrian name for pedestrian spells. When I have more skill, perhaps "
"I'll make some with better names. Several suggest themselves: "
"<_:itemizedlist-1/>"
msgstr ""
"För att skapa ny magi skriver du dina besvärjelser där Gnumeric hittar dem. "
"Använd katalogerna under "
"<literal>~/.gnumeric/&lt;version&gt;/plugins/</literal>. Varje underkatalog "
"är en ”magibok” med nya insticksmodulsfunktioner. Du kan samla alla "
"besvärjelser i en bok eller ordna dem som du vill. Varje magibok måste "
"innehålla två filer. Vi skapar en som heter ”myfuncs” – ett ganska "
"vardagligt namn för vardagliga besvärjelser. När jag har blivit skickligare "
"kanske jag hittar på bättre namn. Några förslag finns här: "
"<_:itemizedlist-1/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:805
msgid "Prepare the spellbook"
msgstr "Förbered magiboken"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:807
msgid ""
"In many ways it would be easier to start by copying the py_func spellbook to"
" your local .gnumeric folder, and just adding a function to that. But in "
"general it will be more useful to be able to write your own separate "
"spellbooks, so here we go."
msgstr ""
"Det vore på många sätt enklare att kopiera magiboken py_func till din lokala"
" .gnumeric-katalog och bara lägga till en funktion där. Men i allmänhet är "
"det mer användbart att kunna skriva egna, fristående magiböcker. Vi kör "
"igång."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:814
msgid ""
"<emphasis role=\"bold\">Make the folder: </emphasis> First we make the "
"folders and get into the right one. As noted above, we'll call our folder "
"(spellbook) myfuncs."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis role=\"bold\">Skapa katalogen:</emphasis> Börja med att skapa "
"katalogerna och gå till rätt plats. Som tidigare nämnts kallar vi katalogen "
"(magiboken) myfuncs."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:820
msgid "If they don't already exist:"
msgstr "Om de inte redan finns:"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:823
msgid "<literal>mkdir ~/.gnumeric/&lt;version&gt;</literal>"
msgstr "<literal>mkdir ~/.gnumeric/&lt;version&gt;</literal>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:826
msgid "<literal>mkdir ~/.gnumeric/&lt;version&gt;/plugins/myfuncs/</literal>"
msgstr "<literal>mkdir ~/.gnumeric/&lt;version&gt;/plugins/myfuncs/</literal>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:827
msgid "<literal>cd ~/.gnumeric/&lt;version&gt;/plugins/myfuncs/</literal>"
msgstr "<literal>cd ~/.gnumeric/&lt;version&gt;/plugins/myfuncs/</literal>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:832
msgid ""
"<emphasis role=\"bold\">Make the files:</emphasis> A spellbook has two "
"files. The first is the python file with the functions. The second is the "
"XML file \"plugin.xml\". The XML file holds that master spells that tell "
"Gnumeric what functions we've defined, and what the name of the python file "
"<emphasis>is</emphasis>, and one other important item. We'll create these as"
" blank files."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis role=\"bold\">Skapa filerna:</emphasis> En magibok innehåller två "
"filer. Den första är Python-filen med funktionerna. Den andra är XML-filen "
"”plugin.xml”. XML-filen berättar för Gnumeric vilka funktioner som finns, "
"vad Python-filens namn <emphasis>är</emphasis> och en annan viktig uppgift. "
"Skapa dessa som tomma filer."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:842
msgid "<literal>touch my-func.py</literal>"
msgstr "<literal>touch my-func.py</literal>"
